{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"allow"}],"title":"PermissionEffect.allow","roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK16PermissionEffectO5allowyA2CmF"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"allow","kind":"identifier"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/permissioneffect\/allow"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/allow","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect"]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PermissionEffect/allow":{"title":"PermissionEffect.allow","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"allow"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/allow","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/permissioneffect\/allow","role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PermissionEffect":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"PermissionEffect","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PermissionEffect"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/permissioneffect","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PermissionEffect"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Whether a grant permits an action or refuses it (B1, deny-override). # Precedence Default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deny -> an [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PermissionEffect::Allow"},{"text":"] grant permits -> a [","type":"text"},{"code":"PermissionEffect::Deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] grant","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and beats every allow"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", wherever either sits in the resource hierarchy. Deny","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wins; there is no most-specific-wins tie-break. That choice is deliberate and is argued in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full in ","type":"text"},{"code":"claude_dev\/deny-override-design.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" §2.1. The short version: deny-override buys one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checkable property — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"adding a deny rule can never widen access, and can never be undone by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adding allows","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — and most-specific-wins buys expressiveness at the cost of making “is X","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"denied?” unanswerable without enumerating every other rule that might out-specify it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"PermissionEffect::Allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] is the default, so data written before this existed, and clients","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that send no ","type":"text"},{"code":"effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", both mean “allow”. No migration.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"AxiamSDK","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"}}